  "title": "CMS | Next-year inpatient claims ML",
  "scope": "CMS DE-SynPUF Sample 1, synthetic data only. 73,757 eligible beneficiaries. Baseline features end 2008-12-31; target is at least one accepted claim ending in 2009. Full 2009 Part A, no HMO and survival through 2009 are required to interpret absence as zero.",
  "validation": "Fixed seed, stratified beneficiary split: 60% training, 20% probability calibration, 20% locked test. Fixed hyperparameters; median imputation and scaling fitted on training only. Platt calibration uses calibration people only. No test-driven model selection. This is a held-out-person evaluation with forward-looking labels, not validation in a later calendar cohort.",
  "limitations": "Synthetic relationships do not demonstrate performance on real patients or clinical usefulness. Eligibility depends on later enrollment and survival, so results apply to that retrospective complete-follow-up population. Labels include carry-in stays ending in 2009, not incident admissions or readmissions. Aggregate held-out errors have no external validation or confidence intervals; subgroup scores do not establish fairness.",
